eland outing no longer are you  stuffing your face with every piece of  junk we find before over encumbrance  prevents you from fast travelling home  you pick up that one blueprint you're  trying to craft and you stick to the  materials and entails but over  encumbrance  really isn't the only reason why you're  crawling home there's a fear and running  out of clean water because drinking  dirty water leads to rads rads leach  taking rat aways and the thing is rat  aways and Kem's immediately make you  parched it's a vicious cycle that  formulates a fear of being stranded  slowly dying in the wasteland with your  health withering away along with your 30  minutes of progress and that fear is the  goddamn best part it pressures you to  plan ahead  up until survival mode you were looking  at a map littered with destinations now  it's filled with routes waypoints ending  with a safe settlement to not just  restock but relax take this run of mine  for instance after a night of inventory  prep I wake up at 1:00 a.m. to avoid  ending my run at night I drink water  from the pump I have breakfast I get in  my power armor because I'm a wuss and  then I hit the road with my companion  ADA who carries a fat man in emergency  supplies the plan is to tackle a  sidequest at the watering station do  some aluminium looting and then end at  Diamond City to restock it's a good plan  and it starts off fine keeping my  distance by sniping ignoring the  occasional squad of super mutants  finding plenty of beds to sleep at it's  a breeze then I find these sewers it's  not part of the plan but I got this no I  don't it's filled with ghouls five  minutes in I realize I'm out of clean  water so now I'm drinking sewage I run  out of ammo for both weapons so I'm  forced to pick up and use a pipe pistol  I haven't saved in 20 minutes and I'm  using a pipe pistol to survive I managed  to get out and I check into the dugout  in for the night I put 150 hours in  fallout 4 and I've never felt the pa